## What Did NOT Work (and why)

- **Building a distiller (the handoff's plan)** — REJECTED because: capture hook collected 96% noise (39+ raw `<task-notification>` blocks, dupes, voice fragments; 161 NEW / 1 PROCESSED in 6 weeks); real distillation already happens in-session (proof: commits `38835c2b`/`5075b8df` = inbox entries distilled same-day). A distiller would legalize a second degraded memory system.
- **`.agents/skills` mirror-parity test** — REMOVED because: Director ruled mirrors are not a runtime problem (webapp reads ONLY `.claude/skills`; `.agents`/`.codex` never execute in the app). The parity test guarded something we don't care about and would spuriously fail on legitimate Codex-copy drift.
- **`TZ='Asia/Dubai' date` on Git Bash** — returns UTC (no zoneinfo); silently gave wrong time all prior session. Use plain local `date` / the inject-time hook.
- **MCP Supabase `execute_sql`** — "You do not have permission"; fell back to service-role scripts via `.env.local`.

