## Decisions Made

- **Reject the distiller; learning lives in-session.** Reason: capture was 96% noise; repo-tracked skills are the real cross-machine carrier (git), not a cron.
- **Mirrors (`.claude` vs `.agents`/`.codex`) are NOT a runtime problem.** Reason: only `select-skills.ts` reads skills and reads ONLY `.claude/skills`; the app never executes the Codex copies. So no parity guard — Claude works, Codex audits. (Director ruling.)
- **STUB → DRAFT, not ACTIVE.** Reason: the two are self-declared placeholders ("full impl Sprint 5"); flipping to ACTIVE would inject stub text into agents.
- **Fix reach at the ARCHIVE-parse layer, not a new collector.** Reason: Reporting CSVs are already polled + stored in `channel_reports`; the gap was reading them back, not fetching.
- **Time via hook, not discipline.** Reason: 3 fabrication incidents; process-first beats willpower.
- **Loud-failure = a detector, not hygiene.** Reason: it caught `sandy-gag-library` dead on the first run.

